Third-party material
--------------------

None. Every file in this repository is original work by the copyright holder
above, and no asset packs, texture packs, model libraries or other external
media were used. Specifically:

  mods/doggiowars/models/doggiowars_fighter_01.obj
      Hand-written OBJ — a 17-vertex placeholder fuselage authored directly
      as text for this game.

  mods/doggiowars/textures/*.png
      Generated 16x16 PNGs: flat colour fills and procedural per-pixel noise,
      produced for this game.

  mods/dw_nodes/textures/dwn_*.png
      Textures for the nodes the terrain is built from (dw_nodes:*, which
      replaced the minetest_game blocks the game used to require). Drawn
      procedurally by tools/gen_textures.py using nothing but the Python
      standard library — no minetest_game texture, and no other third-party
      image, was copied, traced or sampled. Re-runnable: the generator is
      deterministic, so the committed PNGs can be reproduced byte for byte.

  menu/*.png
      Crops and downscales of screenshot.png (see above), made with sips.

  screenshot.png
      In-game capture of this mod.

The mod depends on Minetest Game (`default`, and optionally `flowers` and
`fire`) at runtime and references some of its nodes and textures by name, but
ships no copy of them; Minetest Game is licensed separately by its own
authors and is not redistributed here.

Historical note: the development plan kept in Prompts/ proposed sourcing a
fighter model and terrain textures from Kenney.nl (CC0). That was a sketch
written before implementation and was not followed — no Kenney material, and
no other third-party material, was ever added to this repository.
